//? Title: Softmax Digit Classification: A Linear Readout
//? Subtitle: Logits may shift together without changing class probabilities
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A flattened digit image must be mapped to one of ten classes. A linear softmax readout provides
a simple baseline with an explicit probability normalization and cross-entropy objective.
We derive its score on three logits, then run a fixed offline demonstration on the bundled
8×8 digits data. The original full 28×28 MNIST program remains available separately. The report shows every minibatch Adam update.
)
\toc

> The method

A D-pixel input produces K logits z=xW+b. Stable softmax subtracts their maximum before
exponentiating; adding a common constant leaves probabilities unchanged. For class c,

$$
p_j=\frac{e^{z_j-\max z}}{\sum_l e^{z_l-\max z}},\qquad
\ell=-\log p_c,\qquad \partial_{z_j}\ell=p_j-\mathbf1[j=c].
$$
\alttext(Softmax normalises shifted exponentials, cross entropy is the negative log probability of the true class, and its logit gradient is probability minus the one-hot label.)

The linear model has DK+K learned scalars: 7850 for MNIST's 784 pixels and 10 classes,
or 650 for 64 bundled digit pixels. Decision boundaries are affine in the pixel features.
Training costs O(NDK) per epoch. The executed model creates a tensor ParameterStore and exposes its affine logits,
minibatch Adam objective and every update. Pixel intensities divide by the known maximum 16. It is an offline
method demonstration, not a reproduction of the original program's Adam/validation-selected
MNIST benchmark. Use `just run-nn softmax_mnist` with prepared MNIST files for that workflow.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/softmax_mnist_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/softmax_mnist_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/softmax_mnist_concept.tikz > build/softmax_mnist_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/softmax_mnist_concept.svg build/softmax_mnist_concept.dvi > build/softmax_mnist_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/softmax_mnist_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
