\caption(Training loss on the bundled 8×8 digits; held-out scores are evaluated after the fixed training budget.)
\alttext(Training loss on the bundled 8×8 digits; held-out scores are evaluated after the fixed training budget.)


> Conclusion

The exact score and common-shift symmetry agree with the analytic softmax. The offline digits
fit measures a linear baseline on a clearly specified dataset and split. A full MNIST result,
validation-selected checkpoint or comparison with a nonlinear model requires that separate workflow.

> References

- [TensorFlow sparse softmax cross entropy](https://www.tensorflow.org/api_docs/python/tf/nn/sparse_softmax_cross_entropy_with_logits).
- [Scikit-learn bundled digits dataset](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.datasets.load_digits.html).
